# No CDN For Production Assets

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Policy

- **Production** (anything shipped to browsers or enforced at runtime for user-facing responses) must **not** load **executable or author-controlled layout assets** from public third-party CDNs: scripts, ES modules, stylesheets, or webfonts.
- **Preferred pattern:** `npm` dependencies built into the Vite bundle / Django `staticfiles` (`'self'`), same as Bokeh loaded from `@bokeh/bokehjs` in the SPA bundle.
- **Tests and tooling** may use CDNs when necessary (e.g. Playwright loading Bokeh from jsDelivr because jsdom lacks canvas). Restrict those URLs to **`**/tests/**`**, **`test_*.py`**, **`*.test.js`**, **`*.test.jsx`**, and similar—never to templates, middleware, SPA app source, or service configs that define what end users load.

## What counts as production

- Django **middleware** (CSP headers), views, and templates served to users.
- React/Vite **application source** under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/` and production **`index.html`** (built output under `static/frontend/`).
- Nginx/site configs that inject or proxy **external** script/style/font URLs to clients.
- **Not** production: unit/integration E2E tests, Cursor rules, `docs/TESTING.md` examples, pipeline fixtures.

## CSP relationship

- Do **not** add new `script-src`, `style-src`, or `font-src` entries for arbitrary CDNs to ship a feature. If an API needs a new host, use **`connect-src`** (or document server-side-only calls) per `react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`, not asset CDNs.
- Tightening CSP by removing unused CDN origins is encouraged when the underlying `@import` / `<link>` is removed.

## Repository scan (inventory)

| Location | CDN / third-party host | Role |
|----------|-------------------------|------|
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/fonts/open-sans.css` | **None** | Imports **`@fontsource/open-sans`** subsets (**latin** + **latin-ext**, 400/700 + italics). Vite copies **woff2/woff** into **`hpcperfstats_site/static/frontend/assets/`** with hashed names; `@font-face` URLs use **`/static/frontend/assets/...`** (same origin as the SPA, served like other built static files). |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/bootswatch-spacelab.scss` | **None** | Spacelab SCSS with **`$web-font-path: false`** so Bootswatch does not emit a Google Fonts **`@import`**. **`$font-family-sans-serif`** still leads with **Open Sans**, satisfied by the Fontsource bundle above. |
| `hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/middleware.py` | **None** for fonts | CSP uses **`font-src 'self' data:`** and **`style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'`** without `fonts.googleapis.com` / `fonts.gstatic.com`. |
| `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/tests/test_bokeh_job_list_embed_browser_e2e.py` | **`cdn.jsdelivr.net`** (`@bokeh/bokehjs`) | **Test-only** Playwright embed regression; allowed. |
| `test_react_spa_view.py` | (assertions) | Asserts served SPA HTML does **not** contain `cdn.pydata.org` or `cdn.jsdelivr.net`. |

No production app source should embed jsDelivr, unpkg, cdnjs, or Bokeh `cdn.pydata.org` scripts. External **API** URLs in Python (e.g. documentation/search links) are not “asset CDNs” for this rule.

## Bootswatch note

Prebuilt **`bootswatch/dist/*/bootstrap.min.css`** files include a Google Fonts `@import`. **Do not** switch back to those CSS entrypoints for the SPA. Keep **`$web-font-path: false`** and **`src/fonts/open-sans.css`** (or another self-hosted path bundled by Vite). If you add weights/subsets, extend the Fontsource imports and re-run **`npm run build`** so CSP stays **`font-src 'self'`**-only.

## Overlap

- Complements **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`** (CSP and third-party network use): asset loads from CDNs are **disallowed** in production; API `connect-src` changes remain minimal and explicit.
- Complements **`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`** (Bokeh fixtures may use jsDelivr **only** in the Playwright test module).
